reps: 8
vscode: select four lines, Tab
open: customer.entity.ts
vimrc: set shiftwidth=2 expandtab

@brief
Eight times: the four fields on lines 2 to 5 are flush left. They
belong one level in. One command from wherever the cursor is.

@keys
| `:2,5>` | indent lines 2 to 5 by one level |

@hints
Range, then the arrow pointing the way the text should go.
--
`:2,5>` and Enter, `:wq`.

@solution
    :2,5><Enter>  :wq<Enter>

Ten keystrokes. `jV3j>` is five and `j4>>` is four, and both need you to
be on line 2 first. Type the range form until it stops feeling like
more typing than it is.

@start customer.entity.ts
export type Customer = {
id: string;
email: string;
name: string;
tier: CustomerTier;
};

@expected customer.entity.ts
export type Customer = {
  id: string;
  email: string;
  name: string;
  tier: CustomerTier;
};
